  "verdict": "State 1 (the anode not bonded — a Ø11 gyroid with 2 mm of radial clearance in the Ø15 channel): share 0, unless the channel grips the sleeve or ice fills the gap (neither bounded). State 2 (anode bonded, the sleeve free below the bark): the anode bond caps the share at 0.72 (stiff bond) ⊥ 0.15 (soft); at the air-dry bark readings (a bearing of 21–1126 N/mm, which bounds the green one in neither direction) 0.00–0.10; the share reaches `102`'s 0.25 row not below 3927 N/mm (stiff bond); Ta's seam passes k 1 on the sway alone not below 3604 N/mm (stiff bond); Ta's seam passes k 1 with the hot preload not below 970 N/mm (stiff bond), whatever the bond above 4137 N/mm; the centre pad's hot conclusion flips not below 5088 N/mm (stiff bond); the centre pad's cold conclusion flips not below 10411 N/mm (stiff bond). State 3 (a rigid callus tie, its depth from the flange to the install-day cambium at 11.325, 24 mm, the bearing acting too): with no bearing 0.02–0.71 of `102`'s shift, up to 0.72 ⊥ 0.30 at a rigid bark; at the stiff bond the cold pad conclusion holds only while the tie sits deeper than 9.2 mm and the hot one only deeper than 14.1 mm, with no bearing — a bearing flips them deeper still. Ta on the adverse reversed corner needs 0.3883 on the sway alone and 0.64 with the preload in state 1, up to 0.72 ⊥ 1.03 in state 2 at the air-dry readings, and in state 3 at least 0.93 ⊥ 1.18 at the stiff bond and 0.48 ⊥ 0.79 at the soft one, whatever the tie's depth and the bearing. Ti-6Al-4V needs at most 0.55 at any share."
